title: Analytics › Headline figures
route: /analytics
intro: Six figures sit under the filters. Each one has a label, the number, the change against the earlier period in words and an arrow, a line that says what it counts, twelve months of sparkline, and an info button. The figure is a button: it opens the cases it counts.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: average decision time is sample data. The change for 'Last 12 months' compares the last 6 months with the 6 before, and the figure says so.
---
start s1 "Read the row of six figures under the filters"
screen a1 "'Approval rate' 71%\n'+5 pts vs last quarter'\n'759 of 1,070 approved as requested'"
screen a2 "'Denial rate' 29%\n'311 denials · 17 accepted'"
screen a3 "'First-pass approval'\nApproved as requested with no information request"
screen a4 "'Average decision time' 2.4 days\n'8% past the CMS time at Medicaid plans (67 of 802)'"
screen a5 "'Preventable denials' 207\n'67% of 311 denials'"
screen a6 "'Appeals overturned' 56%\n'54 of 96 rulings · 17 denials accepted'"
process p1 "Each change compares this quarter with last quarter, last quarter with the one before, or the last 6 months with the 6 before for 'Last 12 months'\nGreen words mean better, red worse, grey neither"
process p2 "Sparkline: one value for each of the last 12 months\nAppeals use the 3 months up to each month, because one month holds too few rulings"

group gInfo "Info button on each figure"
  click i1 "Hover or Tab to the info icon"
  overlay i2 "A short definition\nCMS decision time: 72 hours expedited, 7 calendar days standard, from 2026, Medicaid managed care plans, 'Check your state.'"
  input i3 "Escape or moving away closes it"
endgroup

click c1 "Click a figure"
process p3 "Opens the case list panel for the cases that figure counts\nApproval rate: approved as requested\nDenial rate: denied or approved in part\nFirst-pass: approved with no information request\nDecision time: all decisions, slowest first\nPreventable: preventable denials\nAppeals: appeals the payer ruled on"
decision q1 "Fewer than 20 decisions behind it?"
screen h1 "The figure shows a dash\nThe line below says what it rests on"
goto g1 "Continues in: Analytics › Case list panel"
end e1 "Figure read"

s1 --> a1 & a2 & a3 & a4 & a5 & a6
a1 & a2 & a3 & a4 & a5 & a6 --> p1
a1 --> p2
a4 --> i1 --> i2 --> i3
a1 & a2 & a3 & a4 & a5 & a6 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| h1 --> e1
q1 -->|No| c1
c1 --> p3 --> g1
